=head1 DESCRIPTION

Describes potential issues found during state machine validation.
Rather than raise an exception, validation will return a list of
B<diagnostic elements> containing diagnostic information.

The ValidateStateMachineDefinitionlAPI
(https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/apireference/API_ValidateStateMachineDefinition.html)
might add new diagnostics in the future, adjust diagnostic codes, or
change the message wording. Your automated processes should only rely
on the value of the B<result> field value (OK, FAIL). Do B<not> rely on
the exact order, count, or wording of diagnostic messages.

B<List of warning codes>

=over

=item NO_DOLLAR

No C<.$> on a field that appears to be a JSONPath or Intrinsic
Function.

=item NO_PATH

Field value looks like a path, but field name does not end with 'Path'.

=item PASS_RESULT_IS_STATIC

Attempt to use a path in the result of a pass state.

=back

B<List of error codes>

=over

=item INVALID_JSON_DESCRIPTION

JSON syntax problem found.

=item MISSING_DESCRIPTION

Received a null or empty workflow input.

=item SCHEMA_VALIDATION_FAILED

Schema validation reported errors.

=item INVALID_RESOURCE

The value of a Task-state resource field is invalid.

=item MISSING_END_STATE

The workflow does not have a terminal state.

=item DUPLICATE_STATE_NAME

The same state name appears more than once.

=item INVALID_STATE_NAME

The state name does not follow the naming convention.

=item STATE_MACHINE_NAME_EMPTY

The state machine name has not been specified.

=item STATE_MACHINE_NAME_INVALID

The state machine name does not follow the naming convention.

=item STATE_MACHINE_NAME_TOO_LONG

The state name exceeds the allowed length.

=item STATE_MACHINE_NAME_ALREADY_EXISTS

The state name already exists.

=item DUPLICATE_LABEL_NAME

A label name appears more than once.

=item INVALID_LABEL_NAME

You have provided an invalid label name.

=item MISSING_TRANSITION_TARGET

The value of "Next" field doesn't match a known state name.

=item TOO_DEEPLY_NESTED

The states are too deeply nested.

=back


=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 B<REQUIRED> Code => Str

Identifying code for the diagnostic.


=head2 Location => Str

Location of the issue in the state machine, if available.

For errors specific to a field, the location could be in the format:
C</States/E<lt>StateNameE<gt>/E<lt>FieldNameE<gt>>, for example:
C</States/FailState/ErrorPath>.


=head2 B<REQUIRED> Message => Str

Message describing the diagnostic condition.


=head2 B<REQUIRED> Severity => Str

A value of C<ERROR> means that you cannot create or update a state
machine with this definition.

C<WARNING> level diagnostics alert you to potential issues, but they
will not prevent you from creating or updating your state machine.



